          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On September 10, 2010, around 10:30 PM, a witness observed for 40 minutes the movements of a very bright object at a very high altitude in the sky. The characteristics of the observation (very bright object in the night, observation duration of 40 minutes interrupted by the witness while the phenomenon was still in the sky) suggest the observation of a celestial object. The sky configuration shows the presence of the planet Jupiter, with a magnitude of -2.9 (observable with the naked eye), in the southeastern sector of the observation location. The case is classified as A, indicating the observation of the planet Jupiter.",
